urrent\">\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"Island\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Ferwater Island</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"Shop\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Shop</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Illumine Designs</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"Price\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Price</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">$450</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"Function\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Function</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Decorational, Lightning</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\n\t\t\t<div class=\"wds-tab__content\">\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Date Added</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">?</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\n\t</section>\n\n\n\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span></h2>\n<p>The Neon Tube is a glowing wire that supports logical brightness control.\n</p><p>Instead of a simple on/off state, it responds to numerical logic values:\n</p>\n<ul><li><b>0</b> — light is turned off</li>\n<li><b>1–10</b> — light is turned on, with brightness increasing gradually as the value rises</li></ul>\n<p>This allows Neon Tubes to function as a <b>brightness-controlled light source</b>, enabling smooth lighting effects, dimmers, indicators, and automated visual systems when connected to logic components.\n</p><p>You can buy it at <a href=\"/wiki/Illumine_Designs\" title=\"Illumine Designs\"><b>Illumine Designs</b></a> for $450.\n</p><p>The placing system is the same as any other item that depends on some kind of wire.\n</p><p>When placing Neon tubes know that:\n</p>\n<ul><li>They cannot be placed on non-solid surfaces.</li>\n<li>The maximum node count for (1x) box of Neon Tubes is 15 nodes.</li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260903163437\nCache expiry: 2592000\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.027 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.035 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 53/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 47/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 28/5000000 bytes\nLua time usage: 0.005/7.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 1019479/104857600 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   28.424      1 Template:Objects\n100.00%   28.424      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key 1.43.9_prod_oaklands:pcache:idhash:3795-0!sseVary=RegularPage!FandomDesktop!LegacyGalleries and timestamp 20260903163437 and revision id 21063. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>","categories":["Schematics","Structures"],"links":[{"title":"Illumine Designs","exists":true}],"images":["Neon_Tube_Boxed.png"]}
